# Files covered here require @lonniev's review before merge (enforced by branch
# protection: "Require review from Code Owners"). Files left UNCOVERED are eligible for
# path-gated auto-merge once CI is green and QA applies qa/pass.
#
# The catch-all comes first and the carve-outs come after it, because CODEOWNERS is
# LAST-MATCH-WINS. Written the other way round — listing only the paths that need review —
# anything not on the list is ungated, including files that do not exist yet. This repo was
# in exactly that state: /src/, /pyproject.toml, /uv.lock and /.github/ were owned, so a new
# top-level file would have landed unreviewed. Default-deny, then carve out.

